WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:01.140
OK.

00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:07.370
Let's go next to our caller from the 773 area
code who's calling today from 773 meeting

00:00:07.370 --> 00:00:10.350
contract in college.

00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:12.590
Hello?

00:00:12.590 --> 00:00:15.730
Yeah, that's you.

00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:16.730
Oh.

00:00:16.730 --> 00:00:18.699
Oh, my God.

00:00:18.699 --> 00:00:20.179
Hey, David.

00:00:20.179 --> 00:00:21.640
Hi, my name is Barry.

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:23.269
I want to apologize.

00:00:23.269 --> 00:00:27.183
I've been wanting to become a member for a
while, but it seems like every time I want

00:00:27.183 --> 00:00:30.980
to become a member, something crazy happens.

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:32.369
Right.

00:00:32.369 --> 00:00:36.559
But the reason why I'm calling is because
of the election in Wisconsin.

00:00:36.559 --> 00:00:40.149
So like I write in to the show like super
tax often about stuff.

00:00:40.149 --> 00:00:42.039
What's going on in Wisconsin?

00:00:42.039 --> 00:00:44.109
I'm working on like a campaign here.

00:00:44.109 --> 00:00:50.070
And, you know, I've been making around 200,
250 calls a day to residents here trying to

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:53.900
get them to get absentee ballots.

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:57.460
And they literally ran out of absentee ballots.

00:00:57.460 --> 00:01:03.390
They're sending people absentee ballots late
and then it's due on Thursday.

00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:09.390
But, you know, people are going to be able
to get sent out and they only are going to

00:01:09.390 --> 00:01:12.939
have 12 voting locations in the Milwaukee
area.

00:01:12.939 --> 00:01:13.939
Right.

00:01:13.939 --> 00:01:16.480
It's usually over 100.

00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:24.439
I guess my question is, what effect do you
think that this is going to have on like the

00:01:24.439 --> 00:01:25.579
rest of the election?

00:01:25.579 --> 00:01:29.600
Like the fact that this election is still
going to go on?

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:30.820
Yeah.

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:35.710
So earlier this week, we did a story about
how Nancy Pelosi is now saying we really need

00:01:35.710 --> 00:01:37.190
to do vote by mail.

00:01:37.190 --> 00:01:42.820
And I fear that this this is going to have
a huge effect is my fear, especially because

00:01:42.820 --> 00:01:49.900
people staying home is is very much partisan
in the sense that Republicans are much more

00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:54.250
likely to not take the virus seriously and
to just go out in public.

00:01:54.250 --> 00:02:00.560
So if we get to November, it is very likely
that if there are still virus fears and it

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:03.890
seems like that's certainly plausible, it
may even be the start of the second wave at

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:04.890
that point in time.

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:05.890
We don't know.

00:02:05.890 --> 00:02:10.250
My guess is if it's not vote by mail, you
are going to have way more people who would

00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:15.180
be going out to vote for the Democratic nominee
staying home versus trumpets who are more

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:17.900
likely to just say, hey, this is no big deal,
I'm going to go out and vote.

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:20.650
So I believe we need to go to a full vote
by mail system.

00:02:20.650 --> 00:02:22.780
All we're really we have the infrastructure.

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:26.650
We're basically just saying let's give an
absentee ballot to everyone instead of having

00:02:26.650 --> 00:02:29.980
to justify why you get an absentee ballot.

00:02:29.980 --> 00:02:38.190
Yeah, I think also the last question I was
having, like my girlfriend lost her job, know

00:02:38.190 --> 00:02:43.280
several coworkers that they had to let go
because we went from canvasing to just 100

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:46.390
percent phone baking and so they don't need
as many people.

00:02:46.390 --> 00:02:47.390
Right.

00:02:47.390 --> 00:02:50.520
And, you know, leases are coming, you know,
do that.

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:52.220
People have to decide when they're going to
move.

00:02:52.220 --> 00:02:53.220
Yeah.

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:58.700
And like didn't like this time is like the
worst time ever to try to find a new job.

00:02:58.700 --> 00:02:59.700
Yes.

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:02.220
Because I've been like looking for different
jobs for her.

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:06.840
And the interviews you got to do interviews
on phone calls, our Skype calls.

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:11.210
You have to get trains if they do hire you
remotely.

00:03:11.210 --> 00:03:12.310
Right.

00:03:12.310 --> 00:03:13.410
Yeah.

00:03:13.410 --> 00:03:17.760
There are all sorts of follow on effects that
we still don't know the full scope of.

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:22.190
Like as you're pointing out on the first day
of the month, leases or do mortgages or do

00:03:22.190 --> 00:03:26.769
a lot of people aren't going to be able to
pay those that will then have a subsequent

00:03:26.769 --> 00:03:29.490
effect and then you'll have people needing
jobs.

00:03:29.490 --> 00:03:31.689
But it being a terrible time to go and look
for a job.

00:03:31.689 --> 00:03:33.680
And a lot of companies are not.

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:35.959
Not only are they not hiring, they're laying
people off.

00:03:35.959 --> 00:03:41.540
What I come away with is the stimulus probably
needs to be bigger and two thirds of it shouldn't

00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:43.220
have gone to corporations.

00:03:43.220 --> 00:03:44.610
More should have gone to people.

00:03:44.610 --> 00:03:47.090
So we can give them more than twelve hundred
bucks.

00:03:47.090 --> 00:03:53.230
Yeah, this the last thing I want to let you
know that my girlfriend was a very nonpolitical

00:03:53.230 --> 00:03:54.230
person.

00:03:54.230 --> 00:03:56.500
And now I have her watching your show almost
every day.

00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:57.500
Love it.

00:03:57.500 --> 00:03:58.500
Love it.

00:03:58.500 --> 00:03:59.500
All right.

00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:00.500
We'll say hi to her for me.

00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:01.500
Okay.

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:02.500
All right.

00:04:02.500 --> 00:04:03.500
All right.

00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:04.500
We'll talk to you later.

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:04.840
Great to hear from Barry in Wisconsin.

